+# AN-900: Record a consent for a person
+
+- **Jira:** AN-900
+- **Gate:** design (trigger 2: event contract `identity.consent-changed`; trigger 3: table `identity.consent`)
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:**
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: worker (wires `InMemoryConsentRepository`); other modules can react to `identity.consent-changed`, none does yet
+
+## Context
+
+The platform records the consents of a person, for example for marketing e-mails. Head office must prove each consent (T4 privacy controls); `identity` owns consents (architecture section 4, T3-D-009).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+| ID | Test |
+|---|---|
+| T3-AC-004 | `packages/core/src/identity/consent.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** `identity/AGENTS.md`
+  - `createIdentity({ repo, consents, bus, clock })`: new required dependency `consents: ConsentRepository`.
+  - `.recordConsent({ personId, purpose, textVersion, channel, granted }): Promise<ConsentRecord>`. Throws `UnknownPersonError` for an unknown person, `InvalidConsentError` for an empty purpose or text version or an unknown channel.
+  - `.currentConsent(personId, purpose): Promise<ConsentRecord | null>`: the latest record for the purpose.
+  - `.consentHistory(personId): Promise<ConsentRecord[]>`: oldest first.
+  - Exports `InMemoryConsentRepository`, `CONSENT_CHANNELS`, `UnknownPersonError`, `InvalidConsentError`, and the types `ConsentRecord`, `ConsentChannel`, `ConsentRepository`, `ConsentChanged`, `RecordConsentInput`.
+  - Invariant: a consent record is never changed or deleted; a new decision adds a record (T3-AC-004).
+- **Contracts:** event `identity.consent-changed`, payload `{ consentId, personId, purpose }`, published once per record after it is stored ([ADR-0017](../../adr/0017-consent-changed-event.md)). No ERP operation.
+- **Schema:** table `identity.consent`, index `(person_id, purpose, decided_at)`:
+
+  | Column | Type | Personal | Category | Purpose | Owner | Retention |
+  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+  | `id` | uuid PK | no | | | | |
+  | `person_id` | uuid FK `identity.person` | no (a key, like `person.id`) | | | | |
+  | `purpose` | text | no (names a consent type, not a choice) | | | | |
+  | `text_version` | text | no (identifies a text, not a person) | | | | |
+  | `channel` | text `web`/`advisor`/`import` | yes | preference | Prove where the person gave or withdrew the consent | identity | account lifetime + 3 years |
+  | `granted` | boolean | yes | preference | Prove the consent decision and send marketing only with consent | identity | account lifetime + 3 years |
+  | `decided_at` | timestamptz | yes | preference | Prove when the person gave or withdrew the consent | identity | account lifetime + 3 years |
+
+  Retention follows the data conventions for consent records. `preference` is an existing category of the convention, first used here.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- Mapping of the T3-AC-004 text onto fields: "type" → `purpose`, "text version" → `textVersion`, "date" → `decidedAt` (a UTC instant, which also gives the date), "source" → `channel`, "withdrawal" → a record with `granted: false`. Reason: the story names the fields; the meaning is the same.
+- A withdrawal is a new record, not a field set on the earlier record. Reason: the story says records are never changed; the history shows the withdrawal with its own date, source and text version.
+- `purpose` is a free string, not an enum; it is trimmed on write and on read (`currentConsent`). Reason: the four consent types are not yet in the repository (T3-O-003 is open); an enum now would guess them.
+- `decidedAt` is the clock time when the platform stores the record; the caller does not pass a time. Reason: the API in the story has no time field; the migration of old consents with their own dates is out of scope.
+- The repository has only `append` and `listByPerson`. Reason: the code cannot change or delete a record (T3-AC-004).
+- `recordConsent` checks the person with the module's own `PersonRepository`. Reason: same module, no cross-module read.
+- Records returned by the in-memory store are frozen. Reason: a caller cannot change a stored record by mutating the returned object.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- The consent screens, the e-mail marketing tool interface, the migration of old consents (story scope).
+- A database-level guard (a trigger or revoked `UPDATE`/`DELETE` rights) against changing rows; it belongs with the Drizzle repository and the migrations.
+- Subscribers to `identity.consent-changed`.
+
+## Open questions
+
+None.
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
